1200 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: Once we're in Stratford we should drive along the River Avon.\That will lead us right to St. Radford.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1210 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Driving like this doesn't feel real... It's like I'm in one of my\nightmares...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1220 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: Believe me, I wish it was only a nightmare. I had no idea the\northern tribesmen would go THAT far...\Susanna: I was going to gather the other dark sorcerers in my household":GOSUB 5100:BM$="in Haworth, and come up with a plan to protect you.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1230 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I guess you really are a sorceress, huh. What sorts of magic can you\do?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1240 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: I can't cast killing curses like the King of the North does, but I can\make all sorts of magical concoctions. I can also cast protective barriers\and something similar to hypnotism, but I can't cast any offensive spells.":GOSUB 5100
1250 BM$="Susanna: Remember what King Hroth said. Only by laying your eyes on the\blood of the northern tribes will the power of the Devil King awaken. If we\want to survive, you must awaken the Devil King...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1260 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: That's why we're going to Stratford. Still, I don't know if I can\actually kill another man... They might kill me before I even get a chance.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1270 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: I think I might be able to combine my sorcery with the power of\the Devil King that flows in your veins. If I'm successful, we'll have a\powerful weapon at our disposal. If I fail... well, at least we'll die together.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1280 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I think King Hroth is protecting us. If those detectives hadn't\arrived before the King of the North, we would have died. I don't think it\was a coincidence.":GOSUB 5100
1290 GOSUB 6110:BM$="The River Avon came into view. David drove his car upstream, with the\river on his right.":GOSUB 5100
1300 GOSUB 6120:BM$="After a while, St. Radford's Church was in sight.":GOSUB 5100
1310 BM$="David: I'll get the car as close as I can. We need to hurry... People will get\suspicious this late at night, and they might inform the Archbishop.":GOSUB 5100
1320 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6130:GOSUB 9010:BM$="David stopped his car near the church.":GOSUB 5100:'
1330 BM$="St. Radford's Church was located just outside Stratford. Being a small\town, it would be unnatural for anyone to be walking around its premises.":GOSUB 5100
1340 BM$="It was 3am David and Susanna took a deep breath, and got out of the car.":GOSUB 5100
1350 GOSUB 9525:GOSUB 6140:ISET X:BM$="The church was in front of them.":GOSUB 5100
